---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { grantOfferById } from '../lib/grants';

const offer = grantOfferById.loi;
const siteOrigin = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://www.wellridgegroup.com');
const siteURL = siteOrigin.toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const pageURL = `${siteURL}/letter-of-inquiry-writing`;
const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: offer.name,
  serviceType: 'Letter of inquiry writing',
  description: offer.description,
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wellridge Group', url: siteURL },
  url: pageURL,
};
const offerSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Offer',
  name: offer.name,
  description: offer.description,
  price: offer.price.replace('$', ''),
  priceCurrency: 'USD',
  url: pageURL,
  itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: offer.name, url: pageURL },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Letter of Inquiry Writing Services"
  description={`${offer.price} for a grant letter of inquiry up to two pages, using your approved program and budget. One funder, one revision, and a clear handoff.`}
  structuredData={[serviceSchema, offerSchema]}
>
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ridge-blue">Defined grant support</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-3 mb-6">Write a focused letter of inquiry for one funder</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">Give a funder a concise introduction to your existing program, the amount you are requesting, and the next step. We turn your approved facts and budget into a letter that follows its instructions.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ridge-blue">{offer.price} · {offer.payment} after scope agreement</p>
      <a href="/contact?service=grant-writing&package=loi" class="inline-block mt-8 px-8 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md text-lg font-medium">Discuss an LOI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-4">What makes an LOI ready</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700">This scope is for one identified funder that requests or accepts a letter of inquiry before a full application. The letter is up to two pages and uses an existing approved program and budget. It can state the need, activity, audience, request, fit, and proposed next step while keeping planning targets distinct from results.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">You receive one draft and one revision. The funder decides whether to invite an application; the letter does not create an award expectation or substitute for the funder's current instructions.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 bg-fog">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">At a glance</p>
          <p class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-2">{offer.price} · {offer.payment}</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-4 text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1">
            {offer.deliverables.map((deliverable) => <li>{deliverable}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">{offer.timing}</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">Start with public initial inquiry information</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700">For the first inquiry, send the funder and public LOI instructions or URL, deadline and time zone, approved program name and short public description, intended request amount or range, and a high-level budget summary. Identify the person who can approve organizational facts.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">Keep confidential client information, protected records, passwords, and sensitive attachments out of that initial message. After fit, scope, and access are agreed, we can arrange a separate secure handoff for approved source materials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">A clear process and timing</h2>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Confirm the funder's stated LOI process, fit, scope, and secure materials handoff.</li>
            <li>Draft the letter from the approved program, budget, and requested attachments.</li>
            <li>Return the first draft within the stated timing after complete inputs and access, then incorporate one consolidated revision.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">The client approves the facts and final letter, chooses the submission channel, and submits it. Late or incomplete inputs move the working deadline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 bg-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">Fit and boundaries</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700">This offer does not include a new program design, complex budget creation, federal application, multiple funders, portal administration, or submission on the client's behalf. There is no award guarantee. Work beyond the included revision or outside the approved program and budget requires a separate scope.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-gray-700">
        <p>Read the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/work-examples/letter-of-inquiry">fictional LOI sample</a>. Compare this scope with <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/grant-application-review">application review</a>, all <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/grant-writing">grant-writing services</a>, <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/pricing#grant-pricing-questions">payment and scope answers</a>, or the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/resources/grant-review-loi-or-application">grant buyer guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
